Original game data. Ultima Underworld: The Stygian Abyss is a separate
commercial game; its name is a trademark of its respective owner, and this
project is not affiliated with or endorsed by that owner. No original game data
is included here. The importer reads data an operator supplies from their own
copy of the game, and everything it produces is written to git-ignored paths
(content/abyss/imports/, local/) and is never committed.

Rune and spell tables. src/AbyssRpg.Rulesets.UltimaUnderworld/Magic/UuRuneCatalog.cs
and UuSpellCatalog.cs name the game's runes and list its spells with their
circles and rune combinations and the casting rules' numbers, as the game's
printed manual presents them to players. They are kept as facts about the game
this project recreates, in our own code; they are not extracted game files.

Reference projects. UnderworldGodot and OpenUnderground are behaviour and format
references under their own licences. No code is copied from them; where a
behaviour follows one of them, the code or document cites the file it was read
from. The sibling repository rusty-dagger (same author) was the one-time source
of the AbyssRpg.Kit bootstrap copy.
